        "title": "State-Space Representation - Modern Control Theory",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "State-space methods are the language of modern (post-1960) control theory. Where classical\ncontrol (Bode, Nyquist, root locus) works in the frequency domain on SISO systems,\nstate-space works in the time domain on **MIMO** (multi-input, multi-output) systems.\nThe two perspectives are mathematically equivalent for LTI systems but state-space\nscales to arbitrary dimensionality."
    }
